<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chur is the capital of the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> near the routes to the Alpine passes. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, recorded from 451, ruled much of the region until the Ilanz Articles of the 1520s, and the town led the League of God's House within the Three Leagues. It is one of the oldest towns in Switzerland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chur.jpg" alt="Chur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amarco90 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Chur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
